MID_SE_Ism_Led_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_001: OK! What do you want to hear next? I'm\ntaking requests.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_002: Ooh, ooh. The song about the hero who saves the\nchief's daughter!
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_003: Do the one about the magical beast that calls the sun\nand ends nighttime!
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_004: Haha, alright! One at a time! I can't play two\nsongs at once, guys. Let's see...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_005: Oh, hello, Promised One. Did you need something?
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_006: <NCA>"I'm sorry to intrude."
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_007: <NCB>"I'm just here to listen."
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_008: <ACA>Hehe. You're not intruding. Please, feel free to\nstay and listen.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_009: <ACB>It's an honor to hear you say so. By all means,\nstay and listen.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_010: I like to sing songs for people once in a while.\nMusic...has this strange power.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_011: It touches the musician and the listener where their\ndeepest feelings live—joy, love, fear, hatred...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_012: <NCA>"Fear?"
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_013: <NCB>"Hatred?"
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_014: Yes. People seek solace in music because all these\nfeelings are knotted together inside them.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_015: <ACA>Balor broke the world so easily... I'm terrified like\neveryone else. So much that I'm almost paralyzed.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_016: <ACB>For my part, it's not that I hate Balor—I hate myself.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_017: I can do nothing. And I despise my own trembling\nhelplessness in his presence.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_018: Aw...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_019: Now, I can hear a song of suffering coming from\neveryone around me...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_020: I recognize it because I had my happiness\ndestroyed once, long ago.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_021: <NCA>"Are you OK?"
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_022: Yes—as long as I have the ability to fight, and allies\nlike you to stand beside, I can keep moving forward.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_023: I know hatred harms the person who feels it as well\nas its object. But there is one benefit...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_024: It gives you strength and the will to keep living.\nI'm proof of that.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_025: Heh. Not to say I enjoy the feeling, particularly.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_026: Even a little criticism is enough to make me lose\nmy temper.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_027: Promised One, tell me, what would you like? A song\nto inspire courage or cheer us to victory?
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_028: <NCA>"The sweet music of peace."
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_029: <NCB>"The melody of your wishes."
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_030: <ACA>Kind as ever. Yes, I want that too, with all of\nmy heart.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_031: <ACB>Me? Alright... What I wish for is all the best for our\nfriends and allies.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_A_032: For peace to come soon to this suffering world.\nAnd now, I'll sing...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_001: You and I have known each other for so long.\nAs much as I hate you...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_002: I didn't hate your song. Perhaps I'll play one last\nmelody for you.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_003: <NCA>"Who are you talking to?"
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_004: Oh! Promised One?
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_005: Hehe... *sniffle* If... If you came back from there,\nthat must mean Balor has been utterly vanquished.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_006: It's strange... I feel a bit sorry for him.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_007: Ever since I first took up Obsidian, I've heard a song.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_008: Balor's song. A song of hatred that cursed the\nwhole world...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_009: I know, it sounds repulsive, but I found it oddly\ncomforting.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_010: I knew Balor was to blame for everything, but he\nalso resonated with something deep in my soul.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_011: <NCA>"Were you talking to him just now?"
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_012: <NCB>"He did support you, in a way."
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_013: <ACA>Yes, I was. To say goodbye.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_014: <ACB>I guess so... That's why I was trying to thank him\nand say goodbye.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_015: 'Cause, well, I can't hear that song anymore.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_016: <NCA>"What will you do now?"
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_017: I'm going to travel the world and try to comfort\npeople with my music. All the pain the war caused...
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_018: I want to ease it a bit. So, basically, I'm cleaning up\nBalor's mess. What will you do?
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_019: <NCA>"Go on a journey to bring light."
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_020: Hehe. I like it. Well then, I'll play a song to wish\nus both safe travels.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_021: <RSDS>You know, Promised One... This is my first time\nplaying Obsidian through my own will...my own soul.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_022: It's nice—playing a song from mine, to yours.
MID_SE_Ism_Led_S_023: May this melody and the gentle sounds of our souls\nring out across the world...